{"book":19,"chapter":150,"context":{"chapter":150,"title":"Let Everything That Has Breath","summary":"The Psalter ends with pure praise: praise God in his sanctuary and heavens, for his mighty acts and greatness, with every instrument, and let everything that breathes praise the LORD.","background":"No title. It closes Book V and serves as the grand doxology for the whole book; the word 'praise' rings out thirteen times in six verses. The instruments span temple music: the ram's horn, harps, drums, strings, pipes and cymbals (1 Chronicles 15:16).","customs":[{"term":"Organs","verses":"150:4","note":"The Hebrew word means a pipe or flute, first mentioned with Jubal (Genesis 4:21), not a modern organ."}],"watchFor":["Where, why, how, and who: sanctuary (v. 1), mighty acts (v. 2), instruments (vv. 3–5), everything that breathes (v. 6)."],"connections":["Genesis 4:21","1 Chronicles 15:16","2 Chronicles 5:12-13","Revelation 5:13"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["הַלְלוּ","halu","H1984","HVpv2mp","praise"],["יָהּ","yah","H3050","HNpm","Yahweh"],["הַלְלוּ","halu-","H1984","HVpv2mp","praise"],["אֵל","'el","H410","HNcmsa","God"],["בְּקָדְשׁוֹ","bekadesho","H6944","HR/Ncmsc/Sp3ms","in sanctuary his"],["הַלְלוּהוּ","haluhu","H1984","HVpv2mp/Sp3ms","praise him"],["בִּרְקִיעַ","birkia'","H7549","HR/Ncmsc","in [the] firmament of"],["עֻזּוֹ","uzo","H5797","HNcmsc/Sp3ms","strength his"]],"x":[[19149001,19149001,12],[19134002,19134002,11],[19116018,19116019,7],[19029009,19029009,5],[26010001,26010001,4],[27012003,27012003,4],[19102019,19102019,3],[19118019,19118020,3]],"xn":8},"2":{"w":[["הַלְלוּהוּ","haluhu","H1984","HVpv2mp/Sp3ms","praise him"],["בִגְבוּרֹתָיו","vigvurotav","H1369","HR/Ncfpc/Sp3ms","for mighty deeds his"],["הַלְלוּהוּ","haluhu","H1984","HVpv2mp/Sp3ms","praise him"],["כְּרֹב","kero","H7230","HR/Ncmsc","according to [the] greatness of"],["גֻּדְלוֹ","gudlo","H1433","HNcmsc/Sp3ms","greatness his"]],"x":[[5003024,5003024,10],[24032017,24032019,8],[19145003,19145003,6],[19145005